Subject: [PATCH] fonts: assume the claimed platform's fonts are installed

Composition offers a font pack without checking the disk for its files.
The operator installs the claimed platform's fonts into the system font
directories, and the browser assumes they are there. A launch-time check
cannot see the host's fonts anyway, since Skia enumerates them later.
The allowlist filter only hides families, so a family whose files are
missing still fails to match on a page, as on any other browser.

--- a/base/apostate/compose.h
+++ b/base/apostate/compose.h
@@ -303,16 +303,6 @@
                                span<const std::string_view> union_array_paths,
                                std::string_view path = {});
 
-// Whether every family in `families` has been provisioned into this profile,
-// i.e. exists under `fonts_directory`.
-//
-// base/ cannot enumerate the host's installed families at composition time --
-// that is Skia's job and Skia starts later -- so "present on the host" is not
-// answerable here, and a launch that provisions nothing has every pack offered
-// with the gap reported. Exposed for tests.
-BASE_EXPORT bool FamiliesProvisioned(const FilePath& fonts_directory,
-                                     span<const std::string_view> families);
-
